# Settings for `docker compose up`. Copy this file to `.env` next to compose.yaml and uncomment what
# you need; `.env` is ignored by git. Compose reads it on every `up`, and so does `make smoke`.
# Every line here is optional: without a `.env` the stack starts with the defaults below and no
# embeddings. Never put a secret in this file; `.env` is the place for your own values.

# --- Ports and logs ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The host port of the service (MCP at http://127.0.0.1:6364/mcp) and of the database.
# MEMINI_HTTP_PORT=6364
# MEMINI_DB_PORT=55432
#
# CRITICAL, ERROR, WARNING, INFO or DEBUG.
# MEMINI_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
#
# The password of the database role (default: memini), letters and digits only. Set it before the
# first start: the database keeps the password it was created with (compose.yaml).
# MEMINI_DB_PASSWORD=

# --- Embeddings ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Off until a provider is set. Without embeddings the service starts and serves, but it does not
# sync git sources, and search answers that no embedding provider is configured (read_source
# works).
#
# The default model is Qwen3-Embedding 0.6B, served by Ollama on the host (docs/requirements.md,
# open question 2). To turn it on:
#
#   1. Install Ollama on the host and pull the model (about 640 MB):
#        ollama pull qwen3-embedding:0.6b
#   2. Uncomment the provider below, then `docker compose up -d`.
#
# On Linux, Ollama listens on 127.0.0.1 only, which a container cannot reach. Let it listen on
# the Docker bridge as well, e.g. `OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434` in its systemd unit, and keep port
# 11434 closed to other machines with a firewall. Docker Desktop and OrbStack reach the host's
# 127.0.0.1 through host.docker.internal without that.

# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai_compatible

# The provider alone implies the settings below; they are listed to show what is pinned. Set one
# only to change it. Changing the URL needs nothing else; changing the model, the dimension, the
# digest or the document prefix changes the index fingerprint, and search stays refused until
# `memini reindex` rebuilds each workspace.
#
# Where Ollama answers. Default in compose: Ollama on the host. Any OpenAI-compatible
# /v1/embeddings API works (llama.cpp, vLLM); a cloud endpoint gets your text, so choose it on
# purpose.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1
#
# The model, its vector size and the digest of the Ollama build the eval measured (Q8_0, as
# `ollama list` shows its first 12 digits). The digest is recorded in the index fingerprint and
# is not checked against Ollama: after `ollama pull` brings a new build, set its digest here and
# reindex. Another model needs its own dimension, and gets no digest or query instruction.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen3-embedding:0.6b
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=1024
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_DIGEST=ac6da0dfba84a81fdbfbaf330198c33cd77c4cdfc53e8bc50eb581914a15621d
#
# Qwen3-Embedding puts an instruction before each query and none before documents. In a
# double-quoted value compose turns \n into a line break. Changing it needs no reindex.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_QUERY_PREFIX="Instruct: Given a search query, retrieve the relevant code or documentation that can help answer the query\nQuery:"
#
# Texts per request and seconds per request.
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_BATCH_SIZE=32
# MEMINI_EMBEDDING_TIMEOUT=60
